 "notes": "The evidence supports a short core (9), not 25: only Karl X Gustav, Optimistorkestern and Arbetets ära have real public signal (Wikipedia views 1-2k); every other work in the list has zero views and almost no web presence. The other six are the fixed points of the main squares and the big centre works people actually point at. Borderline, left in everything: Elma Danielsson agiterar (Rörsjöparken 2023, Malmö's first statue of a named woman, well publicised), Trumslagaren (Lundell's elephant drummer in Folkets park, the 'fifth member' of Optimistorkestern), Frans Suell, Points of View (Tony Cragg at Triangeln), Flyktingmonumentet (Limhamn), Drottningtorgets fontän, Snubbelstenarna. Of the core picks, Människan och Pegasus, Rubato and Ekotemplet are the softest. Optimistorkestern stands on Södergatan near Stortorget, not on either square. Zlatan-statyn is not standing anywhere (stored since 2020). Pojke med gäss in Slottsparken was stolen in 2025. Bobos hjärta is in Alnarp (Lomma), kept in everything with outsideMalmo. Torgbrunn on Stortorget is the subject of an antiracist critique (Hanni Kamaly, 2022) proposing relocation; check before relying on it long-term. Same-name items without OSM ids (Gustav Möller, Mor och barn, Passage) are distinct works at different points and are told apart by their source field. Kärlek utan gräns and Ljusrugg sit at the same point and may be one work; both kept. The Carnemalm 2022 comic-figure bronzes on Möllan (Elvis, Polly, Mjau!, Åke Jävel, Superangst, etc.) are kept in everything but are small and weak quiz items. Gud Fader på himmelsbågen (Milles) is said by sv Wikipedia to be at Gamla begravningsplatsen but is not in OSM or the city dataset; not added. The Calatrava torso sculpture, Spiralen, Rörelse, Sju fästningar, Glasbruket, Vågen, Tycho Brahe and Ordet were not found as Malmö public works."
}